  i The callback runs once for each item in the array.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
    2 │ let reread = [];
  > 3 │ reread.map((x) => ({ ...x }));
      │        ^^^
    4 │ console.log(reread);
    5 │ 
  
  i A spread creates a new object and copies every property into it. Doing this for each item is slow and uses extra memory for large arrays.
  
  i If it's fine to change the original items, add the properties with Object.assign() or assign them directly. Keep the spread if other code needs the original items to stay unchanged.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

